  "scope": {
    "zh": "这是受交互分析五种功能性自我状态名称启发的原创互动做法观察，不是标准TEG3、Heyer1979、Dusay原工具、疗效评估或JobCannon二十题。每组只覆盖本版列出的四种具体做法，不等同于完整临床自我状态；AC也未覆盖其全部反抗与顺应含义。五组频率可同时较高或较低，不假设心理能量守恒，不把一组升高说成另一组必然降低。无本站常模、类型阈值、最佳形状、童年成因、IQ／成熟／共情／健康或工作表现结论，不凭图诊断或评判他人。",
    "en": "This is an original observation of interaction practices inspired by the names of five functional ego states in transactional analysis, not standard TEG3, Heyer’s 1979 bank, Dusay’s original tool, treatment evaluation or JobCannon’s twenty items. Each group covers only its four specified actions rather than a complete clinical ego state; AC does not cover all rebellion and compliance meanings. Frequencies may be simultaneously higher or lower without conserved psychic energy or a necessary decline in one group when another rises. There are no local norms, type thresholds, ideal shapes, childhood causes, IQ, maturity, empathy, health or work-performance conclusions. The chart does not diagnose or judge another person."
  },
  "instructions": {
    "zh": "回想过去四周，在确有相应机会的情况下，以下具体做法出现得多不多，按1从不到5几乎总是作答；只选自己的实际做法，不按应该怎样或是否赞同来选。没有相应机会、无法判断或不愿回答请选择独立项，不当从不、中立或零分。每组四条全部有效才显示该组分数，其他组可各自保留。父母、成人、儿童是框架标签，不指真实年龄、家庭角色或成熟程度。本版不填写对话、童年经历或第三人资料。",
    "en": "Think about the past four weeks, when a relevant occasion actually arose, and rate how often each concrete action occurred, from 1 Never to 5 Almost always. Describe what you did, not what ought to happen or whether you agree with an idea. Use the separate option for no relevant opportunity, inability to judge or preferring not to answer; it is not never, neutral or zero. Each group requires all four valid ratings while other groups remain separately readable. Parent, Adult and Child are framework labels, not actual ages, family roles or maturity. No conversations, childhood stories or third-party details are entered."
  }
